---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Corrections Policy | devsyllabus"
  description="How to report an error on devsyllabus and how verified corrections are applied and acknowledged."
  path="/corrections/"
>
  <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Editorial Policy', href: '/editorial-policy/' }, { label: 'Corrections' }]} />

  <div class="doc">
  <h1>Corrections policy</h1>

  <h2>Reporting an error</h2>
  <p>
    If you find an error in any note, article, or practice question, send
    the page URL and what you believe is wrong via our
    <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>. If you can cite a source for the
    correction, include it — it speeds up verification.
  </p>

  <h2>How corrections are handled</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>
      <strong>Verification.</strong> A team member checks the report
      against the source hierarchy in our
      <a href="/fact-checking/">fact-checking process</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Correction.</strong> Verified errors are fixed and the
      page's updated date changes. Answers to practice questions are
      corrected alongside their explanations.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Disclosure.</strong> Substantive corrections to a page's
      technical claims are noted on the page itself. Typo-level fixes do
      not warrant a notice.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>What counts as substantive</h2>
  <p>
    A corrected definition, a wrong answer to a practice question, a code
    example that does not behave as described, or a misattributed source.
    Not: spelling, phrasing, or formatting.
  </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
